        "content": "<p>ctiller opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14647\">PR #14647</a> from <code>ctiller:fix/epoch-check-fuel</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>When both <code>consume_fuel</code> and <code>epoch_interruption</code> are enabled, <code>FuncEnvironment::epoch_check_full</code> emits a conditional call to the <code>new_epoch</code> libcall at function entry and loop headers. Although <code>fuel_check</code> flushes buffered fuel into the SSA variable <code>self.fuel_var</code> immediately beforehand, <code>epoch_check_full</code> did not store <code>self.fuel_var</code> back to <code>VMStoreContext::fuel_consumed</code> before invoking <code>new_epoch</code> or reload it afterwards.</p>\n<p>Consequently, if the epoch deadline callback inspected <code>store.get_fuel()</code> or trapped (<code>UpdateDeadline::Interrupt</code> / <code>Err(...)</code>), all fuel consumed since the last store synchronization was missing from the <code>Store</code>.</p>\n<p>Save <code>self.fuel_var</code> before calling <code>new_epoch</code> and reload <code>self.fuel_var</code> afterwards when <code>consume_fuel</code> is enabled.</p>\n<p>Assisted-by: Gemini</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 630556749,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791589644
    },
